id evidence rather than reusable state.\"],\"next_actions\":[\"Repair cached controller-test acceptance validation and atomic log publication, then add focused tests covering stale/malformed cached reports and interruption during log publication.\"],\"residuals\":[\"The packet does not expose the implementations of `process`, state loading, or run-resume callers, so their atomicity and stale-state handling remain unreviewed.\",\"The accepted source panel and passing test count do not establish accounting correctness, scientific validity, or human acceptance.\"],\"steps\":[\"Keep the review bounded to the supplied controller/evidence interfaces.\",\"After the repairs, rerun the existing controller suite and inspect the resulting durable evidence records before acceptance.\"],\"summary\":\"REVISE: cached controller-test state can bypass verification without sufficient integrity binding, and two diagnostic logs are written non-atomically, violating the stated resumability/evidence-preservation interface.\",\"verdict\":\"REVISE\"}"}}
